      "model_overhangs_review": "Two bed-rooted trees, one per side hand-pull pocket, carry each pocket's level ceiling (print z 106.999) and the lower part of its R6 mouth round and corner fillets; nothing else on the cartridge takes support and no body is model-rooted. The ceiling band (104.399 to 109.599, 0.08 mm) prints the round over each ceiling and the interface on fine layers; the floor band (9.630 to 14.830) prints the up-facing mouth round below each pocket floor and the corner fillets above it, unsupported. With the height ranges the slicer plans the trees on their own grid of up to 0.28 mm, which takes the plate from 496 layers (09-21) to 983; support stays at the same two bodies. With the audit's 3 mm pocket floor each pocket now stops at x \u00b191.8, so each ceiling and its interface end at x \u00b192.5.",
